# AmplifyUP — use the SDK, do not rebuild it

AmplifyUP SDK (`@amplifyup/sdk`) owns layout resolve, Composer preview, field envelopes, personalization, page context, tracking, and the render pipeline.

Placeable details: `.cursor/skills/amplifyup-placeables/SKILL.md` · [lists docs](https://amplifyup.ai/docs/developers/lists) · [npm](https://www.npmjs.com/package/@amplifyup/sdk).

## Hard rules

- **Do not reimplement** SDK features (no local catalogs, Edge clients, preview frameworks).
- **Never nest a second `AmplifyUpProvider`.** One root provider. From-page `pageContext` goes on that provider. Nesting breaks under SDK 0.1.77+.
- **SDK ≥ 0.2 owns the component registry.** No `renderComponent`, no lookup map, no `ComponentContextProvider` (removed). `withAmplifyUp` (next.config.js) generates `src/.amplifyup/component-registry` — never edit it.
- **Placeables live only in `apps/web/src/components/amplifyup/placeables/`** (registry root, set in `amplifyup.config.ts`). One flat `<Name>.tsx` per component; file name = Composer `component_id`; export a component with that name. Helpers/subcomponents go in `components/amplifyup/internal/` — any `.tsx` in the root with a matching export gets registered, and duplicate names fail the build.
- Pages render `<AmplifyPage />` from `@/.amplifyup/component-registry` (via `AmplifyRoutePage` in the `app/[[...slug]]` catch-all).
- **Trust field envelopes:** `{ value, name, ref? }`. Editable → `<Field|RichText|Image field={…} />`. Non-visible → `.value` (or plain `id`/`slug` on list rows).
- **`<Field>` is scalar-only.** Object lists are `ListRow[]` — map `fields.posts.value`, use `<Field field={post.title} />`. No `<Collection>`. Never `Field` + `render`.
- **One field per binding** — no `a || b` in `field={…}`.
- Empty hide: `if (!fields.x.value && !inComposer) return null` with `const inComposer = useInComposer()` (preferred in 0.2; `isComposerPreview()` still works).
- Search/load-more: `queryContent` + `searchSpec` / `nextPageSpec` from `postsPagination` — never hand-build `spec`.
- Do not fix Composer bugs in this site — uptick/fix the SDK.

## Example

```tsx
export function Hero({ fields }: { fields: Fields<{ heading: string; image: ImageValue }> }) {
  return (
    <>
      <Image field={fields.image} />
      <h1><Field field={fields.heading} /></h1>
    </>
  );
}
```
